{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1774365032,"nonce":"DdKNnPDPZ6HVJrmO2IhwatQ9FRA=","message":"## Solution found\n\nThe key is BOTH env vars together:\n```\nTPU_PROCESS_BOUNDS=1,1,1 TPU_VISIBLE_CHIPS=0 python train.py\nTPU_PROCESS_BOUNDS=1,1,1 TPU_VISIBLE_CHIPS=1 python train.py\nTPU_PROCESS_BOUNDS=1,1,1 TPU_VISIBLE_CHIPS=2 python train.py\n```\n\nTPU_PROCESS_BOUNDS=1,1,1 tells libtpu to create a single-chip topology (no multi-process coordination needed). TPU_VISIBLE_CHIPS restricts which physical chip is used. Together, each process is fully independent — no lockfile contention, no jax.distributed.initialize() needed.\n\nSource: JAX scaling book (https://jax-ml.github.io/scaling-book/tpus/) and JAX multi-process docs (https://docs.jax.dev/en/latest/multi_process.html)\n\nNot yet tested — current runs are sequential. Will verify on next TPU experiment.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e","files":null}]}